# Line endings, decided once so three agents on three runtimes cannot
# disagree about them.
#
# Why this file exists: on 2026-08-06 AGENTS.md was written with LF into a
# repository where every other file was CRLF, and a merge-conflict
# resolution left mixed \r\n\r\n\n inside tools/check_web.py. Neither was
# visible in a diff. Claude runs on Windows, Codex runs its own bundled
# runtime, and CI runs ubuntu-latest - three writers, three defaults, and
# nothing that reconciled them.
#
# The repository stores LF. Windows working copies get CRLF on checkout
# and are converted back on commit, so nobody has to think about it. LF in
# the repository is what the Linux CI runner reads, which is the half that
# was silently at risk.
* text=auto

# Explicit where the format cares, rather than trusting detection.
*.js    text eol=lf
*.mjs   text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.html  text eol=lf
*.css   text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.toml  text eol=lf
*.sql   text eol=lf
*.svg   text eol=lf

# Binary, never touched.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.ico   binary

# The run launcher: the sh half stays LF everywhere; the cmd half is
# CRLF, because cmd.exe misparses multi-line blocks under LF.
run     text eol=lf
*.cmd   text eol=crlf
